#passage(("What you've just done now is, you brought information. You presented misinformation. You've been refuted thoroughly for every single claim that you brought, with evidences from the Book itself, refuting the claims that you made. Then your response to that was, I'm not going to try to convince you, because obviously you have nothing to present to convince people. But either way, I agree with that position. It's the same position I have. I'm also not here to convince you. So you came with false information; I don't need to convince you that you are a disbeliever according to Islam. I've already given you an objective fact. I don't need to convince you with anything, because it's not the job of a Muslim to convince someone else. But what's important now is that I've presented to the people watching why you're presenting misinformation, with evidences.", "I'll tell you why I'm not going to read that Book. And I still KNOW, not just believe, I know it's false without reading it, because your Book is based on Islam, and it confirms Islam as a narrative, meaning your Book doesn't come and say, for example, Islam is false and it's its own standalone thing. No! But your Book comes and affirms the Quran, affirms Prophet Muhammadﷺ, affirms all of these things, and if your Book affirms the Quran and affirms the Islamic revelation, then if it contradicts it, then we have a contradiction, and by default I can reject that claim, because it's literally telling me this is from God, but in the same time it's telling me: it's from God but it's contradictory what I'm telling you!", "So therefore that is the rational reason I'm using, which is why I'm not going to read that book that you presented me. If it's a complete new thing and a completely new person, or whatever, I will ask you: present me some evidences, and then we'll have a discussion on it. But if it uses Islam and affirms Islam, then by default it's disqualified, because it affirms Islam that says that there will