#passage(("Ridvan points out the Islamic view is that the black stone came from heaven. He then says, \"Now, according to [non-Islamic], unbiased, and more reliable sources, the origin of the stone is neither Abrahamic nor heaven.\" That is quite ironic since the unbiased reliable sources didn't base their opinions on any data. Ridvan admits moments later that it has never been scientifically examined. In other words, when Ridvan says unbiased reliable, he means the opinion that conflicts with Islam.", "Ridvan's knowledge on the matter is quite shallow since he conflates between the worshipping of pagan idols and the rituals that are involved with the black stone. At each point, we will answer: is this an act of worship?",), "Farid Responds, “[DEBUNKED] The Truth about the Black Stone”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Leud7hKXiuE", ((0, "0:00–0:35"), (46, "0:46–1:01"),))
