#passage(("The Prophetﷺ said that the Black Stone is a stone from Paradise, it's not from Earth, and it was white, it was pure like the milk, and the sins of the people made that stone black.", "And you had the Companion of the Prophetﷺ 'Umar Bin Al-Khattab, which was his 2nd closest Companion; he was the 2nd Caliphate of Islam. What did he say? He said at the Black Stone: \"You're only a hajar (a stone). You're only a stone! And I know you do not benefit or harm.\" Where is he bringing his teaching from? He's bringing them from the Prophetﷺ! He told them clearly this is just a stone. This is what 'Umar Bin Al-Khattab said: \"And if the Prophetﷺ did not kiss you, I would not have kissed you!\"", "So it's not like Muslims believe that this stone is a pagan, holy stone or something like that. They know that it's a stone; the only reason we do that practice is out of submission to Allah, because the Prophetﷺ did it. And you can perform Hajj (Pilgrimage) without kissing the Black Stone. It's not a necessity. If it was something that Muslims hold so holy, then they would have to do it, and they would actually be venerating it; they would not just say: you're just a stone! You will actually put it high up and all of that. I believe that time I pointed at the Black stone only. So you can point at the Black Stone if it's too busy, there's people. You don't need to kiss the Black Stone for your Hajj to be complete.", "We don't think when we're doing the action that this stone is like this and that. Allah is the One who benefits and harms. When I do any action, just like washing my hand in Wudu' (Ablution), I get rewarded because Allah commanded me to do the action; not the action itself is that which rewards me. So me kissing the Stone is a similar thing: the only reason you get a reward is because Allah commanded you to do that thing, or the Prophet commanded you to do that thing, or he did it himself.", "The way you remove this cognitive dissonance that you have is: you've