#passage(("Touching and kissing is not an act of worship. So, pointing is worship? Is that how you used to pray? You pointed towards Mecca five times a day when you were a Muslim. He shouted Allahu Akbar, not black stone is Akbar.", "Personally, I take this narration with a grain of salt since it comes through the path of Ibn Khuzaymah, who has been weakened by some hadith scholars. Regardless, believing that something may testify for you on the day of judgment does not necessitate that you worship it. One's own limbs will testify against a person on the day of judgment, and yet nobody worships their own limbs.", "Ridvan has absolutely no idea what the definition of worship is. He actually ends his video with the ultimate proof that Muslims didn't worship the black stone: the actions of touching and kissing the black stone do not necessitate worship.",), "Farid Responds, “[DEBUNKED] The Truth about the Black Stone”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Leud7hKXiuE", ((93, "1:33–2:19"), (168, "2:48–3:11"), (196, "3:16–3:56"),))
