#passage(("The black stone in Mecca is one of [CP's] favorite topics. The Prince of deception himself often argues that it is proof that Muslims are polytheists. In this video he speaks about the historical narrative surrounding the black stone.", "There are two inaccuracies. The first is him saying that men stick their sexual organs into the blackstone; this is a claim that cannot be supported, and CP will not even attempt to support. The second claim is that women used to smear it with their menstrual blood. Now, the text does not say this, and I will be giving CP the benefit of the doubt, since his Arabic is quite weak.", "Now here we have the second lie: CP argues that women touch the black stone [with] their sexual organs. The text says it was touched by [al-huyyad] [in] the pre-islamic era and turned black. This word that CP translated to vagina cannot mean that. Earlier in the video he said that women would smear their blood on it; according to his argument there, this term would be read as [hayd]. In other words, when menstruation touched the black stone it turned black. Now, there's a stupid reading and translation, but at least he wasn't intentionally lying. Translating the term as vagina, though, is an outright lie. The correct way to read this word is [al-huyyad], meaning when women who were on their periods touched it, it turned black. Now, unlike [CP's] translation, this sentence at least makes some sense linguistically. Either way, this report doesn't even have a chain of narrators and is disconnected by at least 450 years, so no, this report is a rejected one.",), "Farid Responds, “Christian Prince: Arabs put Penis in Black Stone [Lies #72-73]”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9eQJp1rnHtc", ((5, "0:05–0:22"), (77, "1:17–1:47"), (135, "2:15–3:32"),))

