#passage(("Are these practices exclusive to pagans? Isn't shaving a religious symbol [in] Christianity? Isn't sacrificing animals a religious act in Judaism? Aren't their religious garbs [in] Abrahamic religions? Are you sure that circumambulation is exclusive to Islam and paganism? The answers to all of these are obvious. Do you know what the difference is between when Muslims do it and when Jews and Christians do it? Well, Muslims do it [in Hajj]; then surely, surely it must be pagan.", "[Had Ridvan done] a little more research, he would realize that this is referring to the [Ansar], who didn't live at Mecca. The people of Makkah did not dispute this matter. The Ansar were ignorant of the origins of these action, assumed that it was baseless. It was then that the prophet, peace be upon him, educated them on this matter, after the verse was revealed.",), "Farid Responds, “[DEBUNKED] The Truth About The Pilgrimage”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=A5pXT8y_N7w", ((153, "2:33–3:10"), (253, "4:13–4:35"),))
