#passage(("It's very important to keep in mind how unfair Christian Prince is to Islam. He'll turn even the most positive thing in Islam into a negative one, and this is just a perfect example of that. Notice how he says that Islam is a [continuation] of this sexual religion. How is this [a continuation]? Well, Islamic law dictates that one needs to wear clothes around the [Kaaba].", "This is the second [lie]: CP is quoting a hadith that is referring to the practices before Islam. There is no indication from this report that this is referring to Makkah after it became under Islamic rule in the year eight after hijra.", "And this is the fourth and final lie: the prophet, peace be upon him, enforced [a law] ending nudity around the Kaaba while he was in Medina, in the year 9 after hijra. This was not triggered because of a woman that he saw in Makkah, because, again, he was in Medina. But regardless of all that, let's assume that everything that CP said is true. Guess what? By enforcing this law Islam has put an end to this deviance, by ending nudity around the [Kaaba]. So how is this exactly a [continuation] of this sexual religion?",), "Farid Responds, “Christian Prince: Nudity Around Ka'aba [Lies #50-53]”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7tRR3roKz7M", ((41, "0:41–1:08"), (102, "1:42–1:57"), (190, "3:10–3:47"),))
