#passage(("If you want to be a monotheist, you cannot be a monotheist today with other religions. Other religions will always introduce something else into monotheism. Islam is the only pure monotheistic way of life, the only pure monotheistic religion.", "A person can die without performing Hajj and still there is no problem with him as a Muslim, just because he didn't have the means, either he didn't have the physical means or the financial means. Allah says: (You do Hajj; for those who can do Hajj) (Quran3:97).", "Just because the pagans did it does not make it therefore also pagan, because you had the pagans worshiping God; does that mean worshiping God now is a pagan act? They believed that God is the One who gives provision, they believed that God is the One Who creates. Does that mean now, if I believe that God is the Only Creator, is a pagan worship? Just because pagans did something does not necessitate that everything they did is therefore a pagan practice. So we can separate some of the pagan practices, like worshiping Idols and making pictures of Idol and all of these things, and separate between things which had that actual origin from God: the practices of Abraham ‘Alayhi salam, practice of the Pilgrimage, or the Kaaba and all of that. These are practices that come from an origin that has nothing to do with the pagan practices.", "That's why Allah says in the Quran: (Let them Worship the Lord of the House) (Quran106:3). We don't worship the House, we don't worship the Kaaba. Explicitly, clear in the Quran, we're worshiping Allah; the Kaaba is just the direction of Prayer that Muslims take to unite upon, so we can all have unity when we perform our congregational Prayer.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Does Islam Contain Pagan Teachings? Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0L6bTixTAd4", ((619, "10:19–10:23"), (631, "10:31–10:39"), (648, "10:48–11:18"), (683, "11:23–11:40"),))
